<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Now to determine stability, need to analyze eigenvalues of A for each L1-L5 case</Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Here are the eigenvalues for each case</Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"><Image height="651" width="396" zoomable="false" labelreference="L19" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjLCQtJSZGbG9hdEc2IyUpaW5maW5pdHlHISIiLSUpQk9VTkRTX1lHRictJS1CT1VORFNfV0lEVEhHRictJS5CT1VORFNfSEVJR0hUR0YnLSUpQ0hJTERSRU5HNiI=</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"><Image height="203" width="657" zoomable="false" labelreference="L21" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjLCQtJSZGbG9hdEc2IyUpaW5maW5pdHlHISIiLSUpQk9VTkRTX1lHRictJS1CT1VORFNfV0lEVEhHRictJS5CT1VORFNfSEVJR0hUR0YnLSUpQ0hJTERSRU5HNiI=</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">PART C) Numerically verifying stability</Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"><Image height="451" width="544" zoomable="false" labelreference="L23" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjJCIiISEiIi0lKUJPVU5EU19ZRzYjJCIjNUYqLSUtQk9VTkRTX1dJRFRIRzYjJCIlZ2FGKi0lLkJPVU5EU19IRUlHSFRHNiMkIiVJWEYqLSUpQ0hJTERSRU5HNiI=</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"><Image height="463" width="559" zoomable="false" labelreference="L25" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjJCIjNSEiIi0lKUJPVU5EU19ZRzYjJCIiIUYqLSUtQk9VTkRTX1dJRFRIRzYjJCIlNWNGKi0lLkJPVU5EU19IRUlHSFRHNiMkIiVdWUYqLSUpQ0hJTERSRU5HNiI=</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"><Image height="419" width="541" zoomable="false" labelreference="L27" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjJCIjNSEiIi0lKUJPVU5EU19ZRzYjJCIiIUYqLSUtQk9VTkRTX1dJRFRIRzYjJCIlSWFGKi0lLkJPVU5EU19IRUlHSFRHNiMkIiU1VUYqLSUpQ0hJTERSRU5HNiI=</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"><Image height="433" width="575" zoomable="false" labelreference="L29" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjJCIjNSEiIi0lKUJPVU5EU19ZRzYjJCIiIUYqLSUtQk9VTkRTX1dJRFRIRzYjJCIlcWRGKi0lLkJPVU5EU19IRUlHSFRHNiMkIiVdVkYqLSUpQ0hJTERSRU5HNiI=</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"><Image height="430" width="598" zoomable="false" labelreference="L31" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjJCIjNSEiIi0lKUJPVU5EU19ZRzYjJCIiIUYqLSUtQk9VTkRTX1dJRFRIRzYjJCIlK2dGKi0lLkJPVU5EU19IRUlHSFRHNiMkIiU/VkYqLSUpQ0hJTERSRU5HNiI=</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">The expected results of L1-L3 being unstable saddles and L4-L5 being stable is shown not only by the crazy trajectories in the L1-L3 graphs, but the X and Y scales are much larger for L1-L3 whereas the movement of the spacecraft is minimal in the L4 and L5 cases. </Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">PART D) Integrating and comparing the linearized EOMs</Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"><Image height="336" width="652" zoomable="false" labelreference="L33" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjJCIjNSEiIi0lKUJPVU5EU19ZRzYjJCIiIUYqLSUtQk9VTkRTX1dJRFRIRzYjJCIlU2xGKi0lLkJPVU5EU19IRUlHSFRHNiMkIiUhUSRGKi0lKUNISUxEUkVORzYi</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"><Image height="298" width="655" zoomable="false" labelreference="L35" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjJCIjNSEiIi0lKUJPVU5EU19ZRzYjJCIiIUYqLSUtQk9VTkRTX1dJRFRIRzYjJCIlcWxGKi0lLkJPVU5EU19IRUlHSFRHNiMkIiUrSUYqLSUpQ0hJTERSRU5HNiI=</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">As shown in the first figure, the linearized case is a good approximation the is much simpler to compute. Although the norm difference is not on an extremely small scale, 1e-3 is still a decently small error. The linearized trajectory is propogated on the same time vector as the nonlinear trajectory. </Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">PART E) Effect of epsilon</Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">To determine the behavior of epsilon, I altered the values from -1e-3 to 1e-3. The error statistic being calculted is simply the norm of the difference in the final positions of the nonlinear and linear model (with altered epsilon in both). </Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"><Image height="339" width="707" zoomable="false" labelreference="L37" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjJCIiISEiIi0lKUJPVU5EU19ZR0YnLSUtQk9VTkRTX1dJRFRIRzYjJCIlITQoRiotJS5CT1VORFNfSEVJR0hURzYjJCIlNU1GKi0lKUNISUxEUkVORzYi</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">The behavior os epsilon is expected that the minimum error in final position occurs when epsilon equals zero (that min error is 4e-10). The further from zero epsilon gets, the more error being introduced because of the perturbation.</Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">PART F) Limiting case for linear stability at L4 and L5 (First Problem 3 in HMWK)</Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">In order to numerically find muStar, a vector of mu values from 0 to 0.5 was iterated through. Each iteration calculated the A matrix and corresponding stability, once that change occurred from stable to unstable, that mu value was flagged. The corresponding value is shown below:</Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"><Image height="277" width="207" zoomable="false" labelreference="L39" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjLCQtJSZGbG9hdEc2IyUpaW5maW5pdHlHISIiLSUpQk9VTkRTX1lHRictJS1CT1VORFNfV0lEVEhHRictJS5CT1VORFNfSEVJR0hUR0YnLSUpQ0hJTERSRU5HNiI=</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">The mustar at the bottom is the mustar shown in the homework problem statement, and the mu values found above it are quite close.</Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Further verifying, two cases were taken mustar +/- 0.01. The trop view trajectories are shown.</Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"><Image height="357" width="749" zoomable="false" labelreference="L41" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjJCIiISEiIi0lKUJPVU5EU19ZR0YnLSUtQk9VTkRTX1dJRFRIRzYjJCIlNXZGKi0lLkJPVU5EU19IRUlHSFRHNiMkIiUhZiRGKi0lKUNISUxEUkVORzYi</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Clearly the before case is stable and the after is not. </Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"><Font bold="true">PROBLEM 3</Font></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"><Font bold="false">PART A) Generating zero-velo curves form mu = 0.01215</Font></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"><Image height="746" width="1127" zoomable="false" labelreference="L43" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjLCQtJSZGbG9hdEc2IyUpaW5maW5pdHlHISIiLSUpQk9VTkRTX1lHRictJS1CT1VORFNfV0lEVEhHRictJS5CT1VORFNfSEVJR0hUR0YnLSUpQ0hJTERSRU5HNiI=</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"><Image height="746" width="1127" zoomable="false" labelreference="L45" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjLCQtJSZGbG9hdEc2IyUpaW5maW5pdHlHISIiLSUpQk9VTkRTX1lHRictJS1CT1VORFNfV0lEVEhHRictJS5CT1VORFNfSEVJR0hUR0YnLSUpQ0hJTERSRU5HNiI=</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"><Image height="746" width="1127" zoomable="false" labelreference="L47" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjLCQtJSZGbG9hdEc2IyUpaW5maW5pdHlHISIiLSUpQk9VTkRTX1lHRictJS1CT1VORFNfV0lEVEhHRictJS5CT1VORFNfSEVJR0hUR0YnLSUpQ0hJTERSRU5HNiI=</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"><Image height="746" width="1127" zoomable="false" labelreference="L49" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjLCQtJSZGbG9hdEc2IyUpaW5maW5pdHlHISIiLSUpQk9VTkRTX1lHRictJS1CT1VORFNfV0lEVEhHRictJS5CT1VORFNfSEVJR0hUR0YnLSUpQ0hJTERSRU5HNiI=</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"><Image height="746" width="1127" zoomable="false" labelreference="L51" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjLCQtJSZGbG9hdEc2IyUpaW5maW5pdHlHISIiLSUpQk9VTkRTX1lHRictJS1CT1VORFNfV0lEVEhHRictJS5CT1VORFNfSEVJR0hUR0YnLSUpQ0hJTERSRU5HNiI=</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"><Font bold="false">The general trend is that the higher the C, the less restricted motion is. In the first case, C = 3.0, there are distinct forbidden regions, and as C increases, the necks for L1 and L2 open to becoming accessible. Seems there is a lower energy threshold for even being able to sit at these lagrange points. Jacobi constant is essentially an energy gate keeper and why a lack of stability makes it easier to get to L1-L3. </Font></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"><Font bold="false">PART B) Zero-velocity curves with a constant thrust added into the potential equation</Font></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"><Image height="746" width="1127" zoomable="false" labelreference="L53" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjLCQtJSZGbG9hdEc2IyUpaW5maW5pdHlHISIiLSUpQk9VTkRTX1lHRictJS1CT1VORFNfV0lEVEhHRictJS5CT1VORFNfSEVJR0hUR0YnLSUpQ0hJTERSRU5HNiI=</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"><Image height="746" width="1127" zoomable="false" labelreference="L55" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjLCQtJSZGbG9hdEc2IyUpaW5maW5pdHlHISIiLSUpQk9VTkRTX1lHRictJS1CT1VORFNfV0lEVEhHRictJS5CT1VORFNfSEVJR0hUR0YnLSUpQ0hJTERSRU5HNiI=</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"><Image height="746" width="1127" zoomable="false" labelreference="L57" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjLCQtJSZGbG9hdEc2IyUpaW5maW5pdHlHISIiLSUpQk9VTkRTX1lHRictJS1CT1VORFNfV0lEVEhHRictJS5CT1VORFNfSEVJR0hUR0YnLSUpQ0hJTERSRU5HNiI=</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"><Image height="746" width="1127" zoomable="false" labelreference="L59" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjLCQtJSZGbG9hdEc2IyUpaW5maW5pdHlHISIiLSUpQk9VTkRTX1lHRictJS1CT1VORFNfV0lEVEhHRictJS5CT1VORFNfSEVJR0hUR0YnLSUpQ0hJTERSRU5HNiI=</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"><Image height="746" width="1127" zoomable="false" labelreference="L61" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjLCQtJSZGbG9hdEc2IyUpaW5maW5pdHlHISIiLSUpQk9VTkRTX1lHRictJS1CT1VORFNfV0lEVEhHRictJS5CT1VORFNfSEVJR0hUR0YnLSUpQ0hJTERSRU5HNiI=</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"><Font bold="false">The addition of constant acceleration in x-direction causes a shift in the zero-velocity curves ever so slightly in the -x (opposite thrust). The thrust adds energy to the system so accessible regions now open up sooner. It also seems the accessible regions are expanding on the +x side. </Font></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"><Font bold="false">Additionally, the equilibrium points are affected. The constant acceleration adds in the +x direction, so to compensate the equilibrium points shift in the -x direction. Physically, the addition of thrust requires a different balancing gravitational force which is why the shift happens. </Font></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"><Font bold="true">PROBLEM 4</Font></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"><Font bold="false">PART A) Generating PM map and trajectory plots with 5000 ascending x-axis crossings</Font></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"><Image height="488" width="656" zoomable="false" labelreference="L63" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjJCIjNSEiIi0lKUJPVU5EU19ZRzYjJCIiIUYqLSUtQk9VTkRTX1dJRFRIRzYjJCIlIWUnRiotJS5CT1VORFNfSEVJR0hURzYjJCIlK1xGKi0lKUNISUxEUkVORzYi</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"><Image height="515" width="640" zoomable="false" labelreference="L65" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjJCIjNSEiIi0lKUJPVU5EU19ZRzYjJCIiIUYqLSUtQk9VTkRTX1dJRFRIRzYjJCIlP2tGKi0lLkJPVU5EU19IRUlHSFRHNiMkIiVxXkYqLSUpQ0hJTERSRU5HNiI=</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"><Image height="408" width="642" zoomable="false" labelreference="L67" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjJCIjNSEiIi0lKUJPVU5EU19ZRzYjJCIiIUYqLSUtQk9VTkRTX1dJRFRIRzYjJCIlU2tGKi0lLkJPVU5EU19IRUlHSFRHNiMkIiUrVEYqLSUpQ0hJTERSRU5HNiI=</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"><Image height="424" width="639" zoomable="false" labelreference="L69" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjJCIjNSEiIi0lKUJPVU5EU19ZRzYjJCIiIUYqLSUtQk9VTkRTX1dJRFRIRzYjJCIlNWtGKi0lLkJPVU5EU19IRUlHSFRHNiMkIiVnVUYqLSUpQ0hJTERSRU5HNiI=</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"><Image height="392" width="618" zoomable="false" labelreference="L71" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjJCIjNSEiIi0lKUJPVU5EU19ZRzYjJCIiIUYqLSUtQk9VTkRTX1dJRFRIRzYjJCIlK2lGKi0lLkJPVU5EU19IRUlHSFRHNiMkIiVTUkYqLSUpQ0hJTERSRU5HNiI=</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"><Image height="405" width="621" zoomable="false" labelreference="L73" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjJCIjNSEiIi0lKUJPVU5EU19ZRzYjJCIiIUYqLSUtQk9VTkRTX1dJRFRIRzYjJCIlSWlGKi0lLkJPVU5EU19IRUlHSFRHNiMkIiVxU0YqLSUpQ0hJTERSRU5HNiI=</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"><Font bold="false">PART B) PM Map with a grid of initial conditions</Font></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"><Image height="483" width="769" zoomable="false" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjJCIjNSEiIi0lKUJPVU5EU19ZRzYjJCIiIUYqLSUtQk9VTkRTX1dJRFRIRzYjJCIlNXhGKi0lLkJPVU5EU19IRUlHSFRHNiMkIiVdW0YqLSUpQ0hJTERSRU5HNiI=</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"><Image height="511" width="754" zoomable="false" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjJCIjNSEiIi0lKUJPVU5EU19ZRzYjJCIiIUYqLSUtQk9VTkRTX1dJRFRIRzYjJCIlZ3ZGKi0lLkJPVU5EU19IRUlHSFRHNiMkIiVJXkYqLSUpQ0hJTERSRU5HNiI=</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"><Image height="615" width="773" zoomable="false" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjJCIjNSEiIi0lKUJPVU5EU19ZRzYjJCIiIUYqLSUtQk9VTkRTX1dJRFRIRzYjJCIlXXhGKi0lLkJPVU5EU19IRUlHSFRHNiMkIiVxaEYqLSUpQ0hJTERSRU5HNiI=</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"><Font bold="false">Looking mainly at the {x,v} view we see the spike around x=0 with high velocity values, this is likely a resonant periodic orbit family. The high velocities indicate steep crosses of the x-axis and the colorful nature of the spike in the first plot is indicative of the families robustness. The curves that appear as you tend further from x=0 are unstable manifolds that connect different stable regions. </Font></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"><Font bold="false">PART C)</Font></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">One such solution that was discovered as relatively perpendicular at cross is as follows:</Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"><Image height="43" width="87" zoomable="false" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjLCQtJSZGbG9hdEc2IyUpaW5maW5pdHlHISIiLSUpQk9VTkRTX1lHRictJS1CT1VORFNfV0lEVEhHRictJS5CT1VORFNfSEVJR0hUR0YnLSUpQ0hJTERSRU5HNiI=</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Tighter bounds of x0 = 0.849:0.0001:0.85 and u0 = 0.0094:0.00001:0.0095</Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"><Image height="530" width="787" zoomable="false" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjJCIjNSEiIi0lKUJPVU5EU19ZRzYjJCIiIUYqLSUtQk9VTkRTX1dJRFRIRzYjJCIlISp5RiotJS5CT1VORFNfSEVJR0hURzYjJCIlP2BGKi0lKUNISUxEUkVORzYi</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"><Image height="475" width="718" zoomable="false" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjJCIjNSEiIi0lKUJPVU5EU19ZRzYjJCIiIUYqLSUtQk9VTkRTX1dJRFRIRzYjJCIlK3NGKi0lLkJPVU5EU19IRUlHSFRHNiMkIiVxWkYqLSUpQ0hJTERSRU5HNiI=</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"><Image height="566" width="726" zoomable="false" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjJCIjNSEiIi0lKUJPVU5EU19ZRzYjJCIiIUYqLSUtQk9VTkRTX1dJRFRIRzYjJCIlIUcoRiotJS5CT1VORFNfSEVJR0hURzYjJCIlIW8mRiotJSlDSElMRFJFTkc2Ig==</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">The new best estimate solution is x0 = 0.849745 and u0 = 0.009470, marked in green dots on the projection maps below. </Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"><Image height="514" width="739" zoomable="false" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjJCIjNSEiIi0lKUJPVU5EU19ZRzYjJCIiIUYqLSUtQk9VTkRTX1dJRFRIRzYjJCIlNXVGKi0lLkJPVU5EU19IRUlHSFRHNiMkIiVnXkYqLSUpQ0hJTERSRU5HNiI=</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"><Image height="531" width="769" zoomable="false" drawcaption="false" captionalignment="0" captionposition="1"><Drawing-Root>LSUrQU5OT1RBVElPTkc2Jy0lKUJPVU5EU19YRzYjJCIjNSEiIi0lKUJPVU5EU19ZRzYjJCIiIUYqLSUtQk9VTkRTX1dJRFRIRzYjJCIlNXhGKi0lLkJPVU5EU19IRUlHSFRHNiMkIiVJYEYqLSUpQ0hJTERSRU5HNiI=</Drawing-Root></Image></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Did not get to calculating period.</Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">PART D) Did not get to Part D bug in code that was crashing and could not figure out even with AI tools. </Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field>
